    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3432a310_374926aa",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-21T16:43:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the power button is pressed between s5 and g3, Chromebox EC will jump to RW with a PD contract while AP is running. If soft reset in pd_init is ignored, hard reset will follow and cause power loss then brownout. \n\nThe same story applies to battery-less chromebooks. When batteries are removed, chromebooks have already made a PD contract on recovery shutdown.\n\nSo, I think we need to jump on S5 for Chromeboxes and better do so for Chromebooks as well. Only Waddledee will take this change as a workaround and we will fix the root cause.\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "79d29c27_46f4b17a",
      "revId": "4d8cb2ab91e292591a66f2ba69050e456c0f8f0a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3788042f_bb9e7ac3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-21T17:21:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What code would make the EC jump on the power button press in S5 for a chromebox? \n\nFor the specific case of sysjumping with no battery, I\u0027m working on a CL right now to just disable the PE layer if we reach the point of wanting to send a hard reset on our active charge port with no battery.  We can continue to sink power, but wouldn\u0027t need to try maintaining all of our previous role information.\n\nI can keep trying to debug why we lose our power signals when we sysjump from S5, and ultimately it would be good to why this is happening on our dedede boards.",
      "parentUuid": "3432a310_374926aa",
      "revId": "4d8cb2ab91e292591a66f2ba69050e456c0f8f0a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d52075a_fb5d90e8",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-21T18:27:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What code would make the EC jump on the power button press in S5 for a chromebox?\n\n1. Recovery screen.\n2. PB press to shutdown.\n3. Enters S5. EC is in RO with a PD contract.\n4. PB press.\n5. AP boots and send sysjump to EC.\n6. EC jumps to RW with a PD contract.\n7. soft reset, hard reset, brownout, ...\n\n\u003e I\u0027m working on a CL right now to just disable the PE layer if we reach the point of wanting to send a hard reset on our active charge port with no battery.\n\nWhat do you mean by \u0027disable the PE layer\u0027? Maybe we\u0027re making things unnecessarily complex and creating more corner cases?",
      "parentUuid": "3788042f_bb9e7ac3",
      "revId": "4d8cb2ab91e292591a66f2ba69050e456c0f8f0a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed8f6244_081cd90a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-21T20:32:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the current code\u0027s assumption that the board wouldn\u0027t brown out after hard resetting if the AP is off?  It seems like regardless of the timing for the sysjump, we could end up in a possible brown out if we have no battery and we want to head into RW.  Though I suppose browning out in S5 might be less customer visible? \n\nGenerally, does the EC get reset after recovery?  Or does it depend on whether the EC RW image changed? \n\nWhen the PE layer determined it reached the state of needing to hard reset (usually because we haven\u0027t gotten source caps), I would propose we move the PE into disabled state if we have no battery and this port is our active one.  For chromebooks at least, this should only be developer/factory case and our primary goal would just be to avoid unnecessary brown outs (ex. while flashing an ITE EC with no battery).  The developer could see the PE state is disabled and reset the EC to get back into a consistent state.  I\u0027ll need to think more about the chromebox use-cases and re-read the EFS2 doc to make sure I understand our expected customer transitions here.",
      "parentUuid": "6d52075a_fb5d90e8",
      "revId": "4d8cb2ab91e292591a66f2ba69050e456c0f8f0a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
